    <briefdescription>
<para>Deprecated v5.0.1 names of the logical functions. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The functions <computeroutput>mt::_and()</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>mt::_or()</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>mt::_not()</computeroutput> are the v5.0.1 names of <computeroutput>mt::all_of()</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>mt::any_of()</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>mt::negate()</computeroutput>. They are deprecated since 6.0.0, and are kept for compatibility with the existing applications; they behave as the functions that replace them.</para>
<para>The names were changed since a leading underscore is not used by the other public names. Unlike the replacements, <computeroutput>mt::_and()</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>mt::_or()</computeroutput> take exactly two operands, whereas <computeroutput>mt::all_of()</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>mt::any_of()</computeroutput> take two or more.</para>
<para><table rows="4" cols="2"><row>
<entry thead="yes"><para>Deprecated  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Replacement  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>mt::_and()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>mt::all_of()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>mt::_or()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>mt::any_of()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>mt::_not()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>mt::negate()</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry></row>
</table>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Example</title><para></para>
</simplesect>
<programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Deprecated.</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">t.expect<sp/>(mt::_and<sp/>(mt::eq<sp/>(compute_answer<sp/>(),<sp/>42),</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>mt::lt<sp/>(compute_answer<sp/>(),<sp/>43)));</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Replacement.</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">t.expect<sp/>(mt::all_of<sp/>(mt::eq<sp/>(compute_answer<sp/>(),<sp/>42),</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>mt::lt<sp/>(compute_answer<sp/>(),<sp/>43)));</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para>The overloaded logical operators of the <computeroutput>micro_test_plus::operators</computeroutput> namespace are also deprecated since 6.0.0, in favour of the same replacement functions.  </para>
    </detaileddescription>
